1. Problem Statement

Write a C++ program to perform level-order traversal of a binary tree using a queue and display the nodes level by level.

Definition: Level-order traversal is a tree traversal technique in which nodes are visited level by level, starting from the root node and moving from left to right at each level. It uses a queue (FIFO) data structure.


2. Algorithm

Start.

Create a binary tree with a root node.

Create an empty queue.

Insert the root node into the queue.

Repeat while the queue is not empty:

Remove the front node from the queue.

Display its data.

If the node has a left child, insert it into the queue.

If the node has a right child, insert it into the queue.

Stop.


